{{Codex|Advances on microelectronics have improved a Corpus classic. Tenet Glaxion’s photon beam strikes up to four enemies at once. It also boasts superior Damage, Critical Chance, and Status Chance.}}
The '''Tenet Glaxion''' is the [[Tenet]] variant of the {{Weapon|Glaxion}} {{D|Cold}} beam. In addition to being a direct upgrade, the Tenet Glaxion's beam has gained the ability to chain between multiple enemies.

==Characteristics==
*This weapon deals {{D|Cold}} damage.
*Beam can chain up to '''3''' nearby enemies within '''8''' meters from each other, with each chain doing '''50%''' of the previous chain's damage. 
**Enemy corpses will still allow the beam to connect to nearby enemies.
**Each enemy hit by the main beam from [[Punch Through]] can generate a new set of 3 chains.
*Can use the Glaxion-exclusive {{M|Photon Overcharge}} mod.
*Adversary Weapon:
**Comes with an additional bonus {{D|Impact}}, {{D|Heat}}, {{D|Cold}}, {{D|Electricity}}, {{D|Toxin}}, {{D|Magnetic}}, or {{D|Radiation}} damage, based on the Sister's [[Adversary System/Progenitor|progenitor Warframe]], which increases the listed base damage of the weapon by 25%-60%.
***[[Valence Fusion]] can optionally change the resulting output damage type, and can upgrade the bonus increase (up to 60%).
**[[Polarization|Polarizing]] the weapon increases its max [[rank]] by '''2''', capping at rank '''40''' after '''5''' polarizations, granting the weapon additional mod capacity.
**{{Resource|Elemental Vice}} can be applied to the weapon after it has reached rank 40, allowing the bonus damage type to be swapped freely.
**Listed [[Mastery Rank]] requirement is not enforced - the weapon may theoretically be obtained at any mastery rank by acquiring and vanquishing a Sister that has this weapon equipped.

{{Advantages|class=Rifle|trigger=Held|
*Pinpoint [[accuracy]].
**{{M|Heavy Caliber}}'s accuracy penalty is minimal on this weapon.
*Consumes 0.5 ammo per tick of damage.
}}

{{Disadvantages|class=Rifle|trigger=Held|
*Damage ramps up from 20% to 100% over 0.6 seconds when firing. After firing stops for 0.8 seconds, the damage decays back to 20% over 2 seconds.
*Limited range of 30 meters.
}}

